v.uk/work-equipment-machinery/faqs.htm","verified":"Daily pre-use checks should form part of lift-truck safety arrangements.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"LIFT_TRUCK_08","direct_score_input":false},{"row":19,"status":"PASS_WITH_LIFT_TRUCK_09","source":"HSE lift-truck safety","url":"https://www.hse.gov.uk/workplacetransport/lift-trucks/managing-lift-trucks.htm","verified":"Lift-truck risk depends on truck type, load, route, ground condition, visibility, segregation, maintenance, supervision and operator competence.","quality_score":"3","adoption":"LIFT_TRUCK_GUARD_09","direct_score_input":false},{"row":20,"status":"PASS_WITH_LIFT_TRUCK_10","source":"HSE lift-truck safety","url":"https://www.hse.gov.uk/work-equipment-machinery/faqs.htm","verified":"HSE lift-truck evidence is truck-, load-, site-, operator-, maintenance- and time-specific and is not an exact parcel-level injury probability.","quality_score":"3","adoption":"LIFT_TRUCK_GUARD_10","direct_score_input":false}]}